      {
        "h_title": "Discover Wat Plai Leam and more",
        "main_title": "Wat Plai Laem, Koh Samui",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Spending the night on Bophut Beach ? The Wat Plai Leam Temple is close to both the beach and the village of Bophut. However, you don’t necessarily have to stay nearby to visit this temple. You can book trips at one of the many travel agencies around the island, often in combination with a visit to the Big Buddha Temple. Bophut is primarily known for its charming village and the bustling Friday Night Market, which often attracts visitors to this beach. Along the coast and in the village, you’ll find a wide selection of accommodations in various price ranges. Just a few kilometers further, you’ll discover the beautiful and tranquil Maenam Beach, a must-visit if you’re looking for a serene beach experience without large crowds.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Koh Samui also features the famous Big Buddha statue, located 1.2 kilometers from Wat Plai Laem Temple, making it a popular combination visit for tourists.",
            "url": "https://thailandmagazine.com/koh-samui/",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://thailandmagazine.com/koh-samui/",
                "anchor_text": "Koh Samui"
              },
              {
                "url": "https://thailandmagazine.com/koh-samui/see-do/big-buddha-temple/",
                "anchor_text": "Big Buddha statue"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
